A||||18||lowfierogt||Question for any cops out there?||||5||
Z||000000||lowfierogt||09-29-2001||07:45 PM||||I was going to change my oil in my truck and got pulled over for speeding.   The road was short before a turn the speed limit was 30 then 45 then 50.    I was in third gear and wasn't even looking down.   I saw the cop coming out of hiding.  So i looked down and I was going 45-46 around a turn.   Pulled me over and asked how fast I was going.  I said, I wan't sure.   I think 45, Gave me a ticket for 55 in a 45.   I asked to see the gun.  He said no its not my right.  Im mad.  Is it my right to see the radar?  Should I fight the ticket??  <P>THX<P>  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/87%20fiero_files/Jun0302.JPG">  <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroRacer||09-29-2001||08:01 PM||||I know in the US, it's our right when fighting a speeding ticket to request a copy of the officer's notes regarding that incident.||||reg||6
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||09-29-2001||08:04 PM||||request a Motion of Discovery during court - he has to prove his calibrations were correct and true<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||Her86GT||09-29-2001||08:30 PM||||I know here in Canada if you are fined for speeding, you don't have to pay the fine (which is actually pleading guilty).  If you think that you are in the right, then you should go to court and that's where the cop has to have evidence to prove that he/she knew exactly how fast you were going.  In your case, you have reason to believe the cop either didn't have a radar operating, no radar in his car, or is just having a nasty day and doesn't care about whethere you believe him or not.  You DO have the right to see the gun because that would be the proof behind the ticket.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||09-29-2001||09:09 PM||||I am not a police officer but do know in Pa that an officer must show you the speed on the gun  (this is actually one time I believe you can get out of the car)  You then can also ask him to see the calibrations.  <P>There are different laws for different systems so go to your local courthouse and read the motor vehicle code.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierohoho||09-29-2001||09:44 PM||||In Minnesota the police do not have to show you the radar unit with your speed locked in.<P>If you do go to court to plead not-guilty the Officer will have to provide proof that the radar had its calibration certified as accurate.<P>Our department does this once a year and I believe that most others do it yearly also.<P>Low, what police department gave you the ticket?<P>If you want to fight it ask the prosecuting attorney for copies of the calibration certifications in advance of the court date, if they are more than 12 months old that may help, you could argue that with him when you get them and see if he'll dismiss the ticket or maybe do a "No same or similar in 12 months and it will not affect your record" thats a fine but nothing against your insurance or on your driving record.<P>As I have said before in other posts, If stopped, SIR the officer to death and be appologetic.<P>Show respect, do not lie.<P>We get lied to for a living and hate it.<P>Someone who tells the 100% truth will most likely get a break before the guy who does the "Idunno".<P>If the officer asks how fast you were going tell him as accurtately as possible and be appologetic and mean it.<P>I personally have let people go for doing the above because it's refreshing to not be lied to.<P>Sorry about the ramble, any other follow up questions post em, I'll check back later. HoHo<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||09-29-2001||10:28 PM||||nevermind- I saw what I was looking for.<BR>55 in a 45 is a goofy ticket, go to court and be nice   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 09-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||09-29-2001||11:13 PM||||I dont know about MN laws, but in TN (where I live) and MS (where I work as a cop), I DONT have to show the radar gun. I usually do though if someone asks, but I dont have to. You can fight it if you want, no biggie. Keep in mind however, that you'll have to pay court cost, regardless if you win or lose....and sometimes court cost are as much if not more than the actual ticket itself. Of course if you win you wont have to worry about it going on your record or whatever for insurance.<BR>Actually we dont even use radar at the agency I work for now....oh well.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroGTguy||09-29-2001||11:48 PM||||Also, what dept. pulled you over?<P>I have been pulled over and ticketed 13 times for speeding by County Sheriffs.  Went to court each time.  The officer failed to show every time, and the offense was dismissed.  And no court costs.  The judge just called names to stand, and I stood, and he instructed us to leave as the violations were dropped.<P>3 other times were from state troopers.  Each time in court, they showed up.  Each of those 3 are on my record to this day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>(16-3 isn't bad)  <P>All between the ages of 16-18 in my 91 MR2 Twin Turbo.<P>No tickets since, and I am almost 27.  (could be outdated info)  heh<P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||02:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowfierogt:<BR><B>I was going to change my oil in my truck and got pulled over for speeding.   The road was short before a turn the speed limit was 30 then 45 then 50.    I was in third gear and wasn't even looking down.   I saw the cop coming out of hiding.  So i looked down and I was going 45-46 around a turn.   Pulled me over and asked how fast I was going.  I said, I wan't sure.   I think 45, Gave me a ticket for 55 in a 45.   I asked to see the gun.  He said no its not my right.  Im mad.  Is it my right to see the radar?  Should I fight the ticket??  <P>THX<P>  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Guess you used the wrong attitude on him!<BR>I got pulled over, and didn't get a ticket...<BR>When asked if I knew how fast I was going, I said "Don't know, speedo quits at 85" to which the officer asked if I could guess how fast, I replied "about 125?"...<BR>He laughed, said I wasn't Sammy Hagar, said I was closer to 95...<BR>He said to keep it under the speed limit, and to have a nice day...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowfierogt||09-30-2001||02:34 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by fierohoho:<P>I was in Champlin. On my way to Maple Grove.  the back way.  I was straight up with the cop.  I had no reason to lie to him.  I did have 10 containers of old oil in the back of the truck and looked back one time.  I really wasn't looking down tell, I seen him. I was nice and said yes sir.  when he asked me for my licence and insurance.   I think the guy was just having a bad day.   <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/87%20fiero_files/Jun0302.JPG">  <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||2
Z||000011||fierohoho||09-30-2001||06:13 AM||||Not to get picky, what was the name of the officer? <P>Last name only is OK.<P>I think I know someone in Champlin.<P>Small town, not alot to do, bored cop running radar is my guess.<P>Some guys just write tags bad day or not, sorry ya got nailed.<P>Per the other post, I did recognize you on the bike but couldn't put a name to the face, sorry <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Has no one noticed my sig pic? I thought I would have gotten at least one nasty comment <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Reality||09-30-2001||08:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR><B>I am not a police officer but do know in Pa that an officer must show you the speed on the gun  (this is actually one time I believe you can get out of the car)  You then can also ask him to see the calibrations.  <P>There are different laws for different systems so go to your local courthouse and read the motor vehicle code.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I got a Citation in PA not to long ago, officer said I was doing 76 in a 65 I said I was going the speed of traffic. He said be quiet. I asked to see the gun and he said he wasn't obligated to show it to me. I asked again and he said he wasn't going to and that I just needed to just be on my way. I guess my question is do State Patrol have to show you or not in PA?||||reg||1
Z||000013||lowfierogt||09-30-2001||10:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Not to get picky, what was the name of the officer? <P>Last name only is OK.   <P>I think I know someone in Champlin.<P>Small town, not alot to do, bored cop running radar is my guess.<P>Some guys just write tags bad day or not, sorry ya got nailed.<P>Per the other post, I did recognize you on the bike but couldn't put a name to the face, sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Has no one noticed my sig pic? I thought I would have gotten at least one nasty comment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Badge # 131  don't know name.  I was shocked to see you in Anoka.   I like your sig.   <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/87%20fiero_files/Jun0302.JPG">  <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierohoho||10-01-2001||03:57 AM||||Don't know the guys badge number that I know. <P>I go through Anoka on my way home quite a bit as there usually isn't much traffic on Hwy 47 as compared to Hwy 65.<P>The big pain is getting across the Mississippi in Champlin, up through the lights at Main street then its smooth sailing.||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||10-01-2001||08:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Has no one noticed my sig pic? I thought I would have gotten at least one nasty comment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What, for being a cop?  For risking *your life* on a daily basis for each and every one of us? Putting yourself in certin danger for people you don't even know and might never meet?!   Standing between us and the crazy druged-out liquered up cross dressing three-named rifle-wielding self-appointed messiahs?<BR> Are you insane ?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You'll never hear me give you a nasty comment for doing that, not ever.<P>'Thanks' with all my heart is more like it.<P>(though you guys could stop ticketing me for drag racing against myself, that one always gives me and the judge a laugh, happened twice now...)  <P>Understand the system needs more $ to opperate occationally, it would be nice to keep it off records and things that can affect us citizens years down the road though (that is the big deal...)<P>PS: One thing an officer friend of mine shared with me, when you're pulled over, put both hands out on the window sil of the car.  Just making it clear you're not fumbling for an AR-15 or anything....<BR>(traffic stops can be some scary times..)<P>Shows the cop respect, and consideration.  Two things we could all handle a little more of in our daily lives.<P>What do you think?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000016||Raydar||10-01-2001||09:54 AM||||I'm with Ben. <I>I'm</I> sure not gonna complain about your sig. Truth be known, I think it's cool. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000017||gargoyle||10-01-2001||12:17 PM||||Hey there fierohoho, I like the sig. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> It is very different and it is suppose to be your sig and that does represent you. <BR>To others, on that rare occasion of a stop if it is at night the the first thing I do is turn on all the inside light and open the window. It also helps to have you id stuff out when the officer gets to your side. I think this puts them more at ease.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000018||Fierowrecker||10-01-2001||08:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gargoyle:<BR><B>Hey there fierohoho, I like the sig.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> It is very different and it is suppose to be your sig and that does represent you. <BR>To others, on that rare occasion of a stop if it is at night the the first thing I do is turn on all the inside light and open the window. It also helps to have you id stuff out when the officer gets to your side. I think this puts them more at ease.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I dunno, I always do as I am told!<BR>I pulled over for a cruser one time in Arizona, cop gets out draws his gun and shouts out "There is a robery going on inside! Get the f*** outta here!", he didn't have to repeat it!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
